cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use JAXTPC in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "JAXTPC: GPU-accelerated, differentiable liquid-argon TPC detector simulation in JAX"
abstract: >-
  JAXTPC is a GPU-accelerated physics simulation framework for modeling liquid
  argon Time Projection Chambers (TPCs) used in neutrino experiments. It
  simulates the full detector response chain (charge recombination, electron
  drift with lifetime attenuation, diffusion-convolved wire/pixel response,
  electronics shaping, noise, and ADC digitization) for arbitrary multi-volume
  detector geometries with wire or pixel readout, and provides a differentiable
  forward path for gradient-based optimization and reconstruction.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Alterkait
    given-names: Omar
    email: omar.alterkait@tufts.edu
    affiliation: Tufts University
repository-code: "https://github.com/DeepLearnPhysics/JAXTPC"
version: "0.9.0"
keywords:
  - neutrino
  - LArTPC
  - detector simulation
  - JAX
  - differentiable simulation
